    "word_count": 104,
    "html": "<p>Hotelier Michael Walsh backed a partnership designed to help people leaving prison find work. In a letter supporting Trinity Services Group's Work, Feed, Succeed programme, he committed Ocean Properties to offering graduates interviews for suitable vacancies. The proposed opportunities included food service, housekeeping, maintenance and construction, linking training to potential employment.</p>\r\n<p>He has also supported fundraising for children's organisations through OPL Charities. Its longstanding golf tournament brought together business sponsors, players and families, raising funds for national foundations and local services. Beneficiaries included Camp Boggy Creek, which provides free camp experiences for children with serious illnesses, and organisations serving young people in Sarasota County.</p>\r\n"
  },
